43 true] [17592186671917 1071 "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'+12 xy=0$ for $y\\ne0.$" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671917 1072 #uuid "2979f6cd-5c5b-5031-9aef-e33515fe3ba1" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671917 1074 "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'+12 xy=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+12 xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 12 xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- 12 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (- 12 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (- 12 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =- 6 x^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=- 6 x^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =- 6 x^{2}+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{- 6 x^{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{- 6 x^{2}}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{- 6 x^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{- 6 x^{2}}.\n$$" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671918 1080 "y=K e^{- 12 x}" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671918 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671918 1083 #uuid "314ddc43-96f1-59a8-8023-3bb59824bbd7" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671919 1080 "y=K e^{- 6 x^{2}}" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671919 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671919 1083 #uuid "3cd63917-a749-555a-bf9d-2fac66925065" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671920 1080 "y=K e^{2 x^{2}}" 13194139538682 1759218