rue] [17592186671923 1080 "y=K e^{6 x^{2}}" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671923 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671923 1083 #uuid "504849f0-11de-50f0-9d0f-349aab8ada59" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671924 1080 "y=K e^{- x}" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671924 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671924 1083 #uuid "56ae88cd-afef-5b6b-abda-e32d3d00029b" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671925 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671913 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671925 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671925 1071 "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'+xy=0$ for $y\\ne0.$" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671925 1072 #uuid "63d7f230-b140-54c5-82dd-72d37987d264" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671925 1074 "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'+xy=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (- x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (- x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =- \\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=- \\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =- \\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{2}}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{- \\frac{x^{2}}{2}}.\n$$" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671926 1068 #edb/ref 17592186671915 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671926 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671926 1071 "Find the general solution to the differential equation $y'-xy=0$ for $y\\ne0.$" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671926 1072 #uuid "673675bd-5c68-5cda-a7b2-bd4261ad478c" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671926 1074 "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'-xy=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-xy & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =xy \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\ln|y| & =\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\ln|y|=\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C.\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\ln|y| & =\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ |y| & =e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C} \\\\ |y| & =e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{2}}\\cdot e^C \\\\ |y| & =K e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=e^C$ and $K>0.$\n\nWe can drop the absolute value bars by allowing $K$ to be either positive or negative. Therefore, the most general solution is\n\n$$\ny=K e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{2}}.\n$$" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671927 1080 "y=K e^{4 x}" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671927 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671927 1083 #uuid "8493af28-b3ab-5643-8356-07d1df783a26" 13194139538682 17592186045443 true] [17592186671928 1